{"Federated credential parse crash: After storing recovery codes in user storage, UI/authentication code may retrieve a federated CredentialModel that is empty (provider didn't override getCredentials) or metadata-only (missing secretData/credentialData) and then call Optional.get() / createFromCredentialModel(), causing login/setup flows to fail with runtime exceptions": 0.8547214269638062, "Stale local codes remain valid: When recovery codes are successfully created in user storage, existing locally stored recovery-code credentials are not removed, so old local recovery codes can remain valid alongside the new user-storage credential": 0.8745591044425964, "User-storage codes not removed: When recovery codes are exhausted, RecoveryAuthnCodesFormAuthenticator calls removeStoredCredentialById(), but for federated users this removes from Keycloak's credential store (federated DB) rather than the external user storage, so the user-storage credential is not actually removed/disabled": 0.8187363147735596, "Nullable provider dereference: CredentialHelper.createRecoveryCodesCredential unconditionally dereferences the RecoveryAuthnCodesCredentialProvider fetched by hard-coded id, so a missing/unsupported provider will cause a NullPointerException when falling back to local storage creation": 0.668057918548584}